note ---- the diff of a bundle-backed item (SPEC section 4), made once and kept as the cache file
note <data>pdiff/<owner>/<repo>/<id>: derived data outside the item folder, safe to delete
note pabcat: git --git-dir=<store> cat-file -e <base>^{commit} for the loaded item's base (gpbase),
note fexec's answer: 0 the project's git store holds the base commit, above 0 it does not, below 0
note git did not run. One check for the diff (pabdiff) and for the JSON documents (pajdun)
fn pabcat to long
pakst
fka tpcatf
fka tpde
fkopen
pakbase
fkt tpcmt
ret fexec PATMO
end
note pabbig: leave the marker <data>pdiff/<owner>/<repo>/<id>.big, an empty file created exclusively
note (one that is there stays; a failure leaves none and the next attempt tries again): the bundle
note diff of item gpid was cut at 16 MiB. Derived data like the cache file, safe to delete
fn pabbig to void
if not pamkpd
ret
end
papdfg
x = pawf 6 0
end
note pabst: what the cache folder says of the loaded bundle-backed item, without running git: 0 the
note cache file is there, 2 the marker is there, 9 neither
